airControl PROJECT CONTEXT
Updated: 2026-09-19
Current project line: airControl v4.1.0

PURPOSE
airControl is a desktop controller for Linkplay/WiiM/Arylic-family audio devices (tested/targeted chip families include A31, A33, A97, A98). The current desktop implementation is React + Vite with Electron for macOS and Windows. Mobile is postponed.

ARCHITECTURE / DESIGN RULES
- Shared React/Vite UI.
- Shared device API layer and shared EQ / Room EQ algorithms.
- Electron desktop layer for macOS and Windows.
- Future mobile layer should be separate (likely Capacitor) for iOS/Android.
- Do not embed Electron-specific functionality directly in React components.
- Isolate platform-dependent features: device HTTP/HTTPS transport, microphone/audio permissions, local-network access/discovery, local HTTP media server, and test stubs.
- Preserve working behavior when adding chip-specific support; especially do not regress A31 while working on A33/A97/A98.
- App version shown next to the airControl title must match package/ZIP release version. Version text is approximately half the title font size.

