A31 STATIC IP / DHCP — CONFIRMED
A31 old API uses httpapi.asp command syntax.
Read:
  getStaticIP
Observed mode values:
- wifi:"0" = Static
- wifi:"1" = DHCP
- wifi:"-1" = Wi-Fi unavailable/not connected
- eth:"-1" = Ethernet unavailable

Static -> DHCP confirmed:
  setDhcp:wifi
returns OK and actually switches to DHCP.

DHCP -> Static confirmed working command is JSON after setStaticIP:
  setStaticIP:{"type":"wifi","ip":"192.168.0.7","mask":"255.255.255.0","gateway":"192.168.0.1","dns":[{"service":"192.168.0.1"}]}
The IP above is only an example from the experiment; use UI-entered values.
When applying Static, the HTTP request may appear to fail because the device changes IP while the request is open. Treat loss of the old-IP connection as expected and probe the requested new IP after a delay.

Old colon form:
  setStaticIP:wifi:IP:MASK:GATEWAY:DNS1:DNS2
may store values / return OK but did NOT reliably switch DHCP -> Static. Do not use it as the primary A31 method.
setDHCP:0 was unknown.
setStaticIP:wifi:1 / setStaticIP:1 did not switch mode.
A31 Static IP from the airControl UI was confirmed working in v4.0.

