LIBRARY / LOCAL PLAYBACK — CONFIRMED DESIGN
The Music Browser/Library is intended as a real library, not only a file browser:
Artists / Albums / Folders / All Tracks, with album artwork.
This model is for local Mac/Windows files and should later be reusable for SMB/DLNA/network sources.

A31 local Library playback method proven:
1. airControl serves local audio over its built-in HTTP server (port 22345 in tests).
2. airControl sends the playable HTTP URL to A31 using UPnP AVTransport SetAVTransportURI.
3. DIDL-Lite metadata is supplied with title/artist/album.
4. <upnp:albumArtURI> supplies artwork.
5. UPnP Play starts playback.

A direct Linkplay setPlayerCmd:play:<URL> could play audio, but did not populate metadata correctly. UPnP SetAVTransportURI + DIDL is the preferred A31 Library mechanism.

Confirmed working Library features from v3.0.7.38-.42 onward:
- local file playback on A31
- title/artist/album metadata
- album artwork
- playback progress
- manual Next
- automatic Next
- current Library row follows actual current track for manual and automatic transitions

IMPORTANT: Native WiiM Home phone/Windows Next/Previous do not control the airControl local queue because the queue exists in airControl; the A31 only knows the current URI. airControl's own Next and auto-next work.

LIBRARY METADATA OWNERSHIP BUG — IMPORTANT FIX
Historical bug existed at least back to v3.0.7.44: after playing from airControl Library and then changing to Qobuz/USB/another source, airControl could keep showing stale Library metadata even though A31 and WiiM Home showed the correct current metadata. In some cases UI mixed metadata from a network track with USB playback.
Root cause: localPlayback/localTrackOverride had priority over polled device metadata and was not relinquished when playback left airControl's Library.

Fix implemented in v4.0.3 and reported by user as working normally:
- Library metadata override is only valid while airControl owns the current local playback.
- Clear Library state when the device switches to USB/Bluetooth/AUX/Optical/etc.
- Clear it when a Network service/URI is external (Qobuz/TIDAL/Spotify/TuneIn/external DLNA etc.).
- Explicit source switching from airControl should clear Library state immediately.
- Returning to Library and choosing a track creates Library ownership again.
DO NOT regress this fix. Do not simply remove localTrackOverride because Library metadata/progress/queue depend on it.

